HELIOSPHERE MATHEMATICAL RELATIONS
=================================

1. PARKER ISOTHERMAL SOLAR-WIND EQUATION
   Type: Ordinary differential equation (steady, spherically symmetric, isothermal flow)

   (u - c_s^2 / u) * du/dr = 2*c_s^2 / r - G*M_sun / r^2

   Variables:
     u(r)     radial flow speed
     c_s      isothermal sound speed = sqrt(k_B * T / m)
     r        heliocentric distance
     G        gravitational constant
     M_sun    solar mass

   Critical (sonic) point:
     r_c = G*M_sun / (2 * c_s^2)
     u(r_c) = c_s

   Fundamentals: Only the unique transonic solution that passes through the critical point
   is physical (subsonic near Sun, supersonic at large r).

2. MASS CONSERVATION AND DENSITY SCALING
   Type: Integral conservation law

   4*pi*r^2 * rho * u = constant = M_dot

   Variables:
     rho      mass density
     M_dot    solar mass-loss rate

   Asymptotic form (u -> u_inf):
     rho(r) = M_dot / (4*pi*r^2*u(r))  ~  r^(-2)
     n(r)   ~  r^(-2)

   Fundamentals: Geometric dilution of a nearly constant-speed radial outflow.

3. PARKER SPIRAL MAGNETIC FIELD
   Type: Frozen-in field solution (ideal MHD limit)

   B_r = B_0 * (r_0 / r)^2
   B_phi = -B_0 * (Omega_sun * r_0 / u_sw) * (r_0 / r) * sin(theta)

   Spiral angle:
     tan(phi_B) = B_phi / B_r = - (Omega_sun * r * sin(theta)) / u_sw

   Variables:
     B_r, B_phi   radial and azimuthal field components
     Omega_sun    solar angular velocity
     u_sw         solar-wind speed
     theta        co-latitude

   Asymptotic behavior:
     |B_phi| / |B_r| -> infinity as r -> infinity
     (field becomes predominantly azimuthal)

   Fundamentals: Magnetic tension of the tightly wound spiral collimates heliosheath plasma.

4. PRESSURE BALANCE (OUTER BOUNDARY)
   Type: Boundary condition / scaling relation

   Zeroth-order:
     rho_sw(r) * u_sw^2  ~  P_ext
     =>  R_TS/HP  ~  sqrt( rho_1 * u_sw^2 / P_ext )

   Fuller form:
     P_ram + P_th + P_mag + P_PUI
       ~  P_ISM,th + P_ISM,mag + P_CR + P_ram,ISM

   Variables:
     P_ram        ram pressure
     P_th         thermal pressure
     P_mag        magnetic pressure
     P_PUI        pick-up ion pressure
     P_CR         cosmic-ray pressure
     P_ISM,*      interstellar medium components

   Fundamentals: Sets characteristic size of termination shock (~80-95 AU) and heliopause (~120 AU).

5. RANKINE HALF-BODY SHAPE MODEL
   Type: Kinematic potential-flow idealization

   u / u_0 = -grad( q/r + z )

   Variables:
     u_0      uniform interstellar flow speed
     q        point-source strength of solar wind

   Fundamentals: Produces classic comet-like contact surface under assumptions of incompressible
   flow and no magnetic field. Superseded by full MHD.

6. FULL MHD SYSTEM (with source terms)
   Type: Coupled partial differential equations

   Continuity:
     d(rho)/dt + div(rho * u) = 0

   Momentum:
     rho * (du/dt + u·grad(u)) = -grad(P) + J x B

   Induction:
     dB/dt = curl(u x B)

   Energy:
     dE/dt + div(F) = S

   Variables:
     J            current density
     B            magnetic field
     E, F         energy density and flux
     S            source terms (pick-up ion heating, charge exchange)

   Fundamentals: These equations, solved numerically with multi-fluid and neutral-plasma
  interactions, generate modern croissant and deflated-bubble heliosphere models.
